{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-gt:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-gt:89934f0e8aeefda835dd6f838300fa8f3fdb4764eba0b402fee83235780c1f88","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:29Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-gr.land","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-gt","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-gt","title":"bob periods brief credits every linked task the whole Pomodoro while root rows split it, so tasks outrank their own roots","status":"open","issue_type":"task","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-04T03:26:29Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-gr.land","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:26:29Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"","design":"","model":"","size":"medium","task_type":"bug","task_type_fields":{"impact":"Review drafters can't copy per-task minutes without contradicting the root totals. Every bob-cli-gr phase from W41 to W27 left those minutes out.\n","location":"src/native/periods/brief.rs linked_minutes / week_time","repro":"`bob periods brief 2026-W41 -f md` prints the root `sase_blog · 1h 33m (5%)` above its own task `sase_pre_blog#^dynamic-agents-md · 1h 40m`. The gtd_daily task rows add up to more than their root in every week checked: W28 4h 15m + 3h 15m + 2h 15m vs a 6h 30m root; W34 12h 20m vs 7h 11m; W35 8h 00m vs 2h 19m. W30's `sase_better_chops#^bugyi-chops` (1h 15m) is a single session that links 20 tasks.\n\nRoot cause: root rows come from the stats `root_parent` lanes, which split a multi-link Pomodoro across its links. Task rows come from `linked_minutes`, which adds the whole `session.counted_minutes()` to every linked task. Fix: split task minutes the same way the lanes do, or label them as unsplit session minutes in the JSON and Markdown.\n"},"is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Proposed by bob-cli-gr.3 note #1, re-reported by bob-cli-gr.16 note #1 and bob-cli-gr.17 note #3, and corroborated by most later W40–W27 phases while drafting weekly Reviews from the brief.","dependencies":[]}}}
